cal constraints on chemolithoautotrophic metabolism by microorganisms in seafloor hydrothermal systems. Geochim Cosmochim Acta. 1997;61:4375&#x2013;4391.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">11541662</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Merkel AY, Huber JA, Chernyh NA, Bonch-Osmolovskaya EA, Alexander V, Lebedinskya AV. Detection of putatively thermophilic anaerobic methanotrophs in diffuse hydrothermal vent fluids. Appl Environ Microbiol. 2013;79:915&#x2013;923.</Citation><ArticleIdList><ArticleId IdType="pmc">PMC3568577</ArticleId><ArticleId IdType="pubmed">23183981</ArticleId></ArticleIdList></Reference><Reference><Citation>Meyer-Dombard DR, Shock EL, Amend JP. Archaeal and bacterial communities in geochemically diverse hot springs of Yellowstone National Park, USA. Geobiology. 2005;3:211&#x2013;227.</Citation></Reference><Reference><Citation>Oksanen J, Blanchet FG, Kindt R, Legendre P, O'Hara RB, Simpson GL, et al. 2011. Vegan: Community Ecology Package. R package version 1.17-6. Available at: 
